  "ssml": "<speak version=\"1.0\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis\" xmlns:mstts=\"https://www.w3.org/2001/mstts\" xml:lang=\"en-PH\">\n  <voice name=\"en-PH-RosaNeural\">\n    <mstts:express-as style=\"cheerful\">\n      <prosody rate=\"102%\" pitch=\"+4%\">\n        Here is your final thirty-second cheatsheet before the quiz! <break time=\"550ms\"/> Single colon means <emphasis level=\"moderate\">is to</emphasis>. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Double colon means as. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Remember the first letters: S in <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"ˈsɪnənɪm\"><emphasis level=\"moderate\">Synonym</emphasis></phoneme> stands for <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Same</emphasis>! <break time=\"550ms\"/> A in <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"ˈæntənɪm\"><emphasis level=\"moderate\">Antonym</emphasis></phoneme> stands for Against, <break time=\"300ms\"/> or <emphasis level=\"moderate\">opposite</emphasis>! <break time=\"550ms\"/> Check whether one word causes the other, <break time=\"300ms\"/> or is a part of the other. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Now go restore that island bridge!\n      </prosody>\n    </mstts:express-as>\n  </voice>\n</speak>",
